# =============================================================================
# Root .dockerignore
#
# The backend image is built with the MONOREPO ROOT as context
# (`docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`), so this file - not
# `backend/.dockerignore` - is what governs what enters the build.
#
# The most important rule below is `.env*`. There are five real .env files in
# this repository (backend, database, frontend, admin) holding live
# credentials. A root-context build that copies them would publish production
# secrets into a public ECR repository, where they survive even if the image is
# later deleted. Secrets are injected at runtime from AWS Secrets Manager
# instead - see backend/AWS_DEPLOYMENT.md.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets: never bake credentials into an image -------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# --- Dependencies (installed inside the image, never copied) ---------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm

# --- Build output (rebuilt inside the image) --------------------------------
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- VCS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.git

# --- Tests and coverage -----------------------------------------------------
tests
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
coverage
**/coverage

# --- Frontend / admin (separate images; never needed by the backend) --------
frontend
admin

# --- Docs, scripts and local artefacts --------------------------------------
*.md
!**/README.md
*.log
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Legacy Python backend leftovers (unused; see .dockerignore in backend) -
python_archive
.venv
instance
uploads

# --- Nested lockfiles that can disagree with the root workspace lockfile ----
backend/package-lock.json
database/package-lock.json

# --- Docker-in-Docker -------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml